<title>UK: Man United jumps to record after win.</title>
<headline>Man United jumps to record after win.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Manchester United jumped by almost six percent to a record peak on Monday after Sunday's win put the football club in second place in the Premiership, dealers said.</p>
<p>By 0918 GMT, the shares were up 41-1/2p to 739, having climbed as high as 745 earlier.  </p>
<p>&quot;You always see a lot of buying after a win. The interest is based on the win rather than on fundamentals,&quot; said one market maker.</p>
<p>Since the 1996-97 season began in late August, Manchester shares have risen by 61 percent.</p>
<p>--Debra Sherman, London newsroom +44 171 542 4026</p>
